        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in children:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " gingivostomatitis and pharyngitis may also need topical anesthetics (eg, dyclonine, benzocaine, viscous lidocaine); lidocaine must ⍉be swallowed, and children must be watched for aspiration; severe cases: PO acyclovir, valacyclovir or famciclovir."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in HSV:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " mucocut: PO acyclovir, valacyclovir or famciclovir; herpes labialis alt: topical penciclovir or docosanol; genital herpes (primary and recurr): PO acyclovir, valacyclovir or famciclovir, most effective if started w.in 1 day of lesion onset; early tx of a primary infect doesn't prevent recurr; immunocompromised, CNS infect or neonatal herpes: IV acyclovir; encephalitis: IV acyclovir for 14 to 21 days (prevents relapse)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Safety:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " acyclovir AEs: phlebitis, renal dysfun, rarely neurotoxicity (lethargy, confusion, sz, coma; USU w renal insuff); acyclovir-resistant strains are also resistant to penciclovir, famciclovir and valacyclovir; foscarnet may be effective."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CI: hypersensitivity to valacyclovir, acyclovir or any component."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
